Ranking correlation degrades faster than expected under item replacement.
At 20\% replacement, $\rho=0.961$ and reliability drops from 0.94 to 0.88.
Critically, simple item \emph{removal} (as in the diagnostic analysis of \S\ref{sec:exp1}) achieves $\rho\approx 0.997$---better than replacement---because the generated replacement items (\S\ref{sec:itemgen}) add noise rather than preserving measurement properties.
Three subjects lose $>$30\% of their items at 20\% replacement, creating uneven construct coverage.
Theoretical bounds are not tight enough to provide actionable replacement thresholds.

